unit PowrProf;

{ Translated from powrprof.h, powerbase.h, powersetting.h and the power
  management parts of winnt.h (Windows SDK 10.0.26100).
  PROCESSOR_POWER_INFORMATION and SYSTEM_POWER_INFORMATION are not in the
  SDK headers; they are declared as documented for CallNtPowerInformation.

  Binding:
    - functions that exist in Windows XP are bound statically (powrprof.dll):
      CallNtPowerInformation, GetPwrCapabilities, IsPwrSuspendAllowed,
      IsPwrHibernateAllowed, IsPwrShutdownAllowed, IsAdminOverrideActive,
      SetSuspendState;
    - the power scheme and notification API of Windows Vista and later is
      bound at run time on first use (powrprof.dll is loaded from the system
      directory), so programs that use this unit still start on Windows XP.
      When such a function is missing it returns ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED
      (the Power* functions return Win32 error codes) and clears its output
      parameters; the fallback is documented next to each declaration.

  BOOLEAN (one byte) results are declared as ByteBool, BOOLEAN arguments as
  Boolean (passed as 0 or 1). BOOLEAN fields are ByteBool.

  The power setting GUIDs below are the subgroup and setting identifiers of
  the Power* functions and of RegisterPowerSettingNotification (user32,
  declared elsewhere); a GUID argument is passed as @GUID_..., nil where the
  SDK allows NULL. PowerCreateRequest/PowerSetRequest/PowerClearRequest and
  SetThreadExecutionState are kernel32 functions and are declared elsewhere.

  Not translated: the deprecated power policy API of Windows 2000/XP
  (ReadPwrScheme, WritePwrScheme, GetActivePwrScheme, EnumPwrSchemes, ...)
  and its structures, the device power API (DevicePower*) and the rarely
  used Power*PossibleValue / Power*DefaultIndex / Power*Setting functions. }

